---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { isoDate, longDate } from '../lib/format';

// Change this date whenever the text below changes.
const changed = new Date('2026-11-16');
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site does with information about you. No cookies, no analytics, and where your email address goes if you subscribe or write."
>
  <header class="plain-head">
    <div class="wrap"><h1>Privacy</h1></div>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap plain-body">
    <div class="md">
      <p>
        This page says what this site does with information about you. Last changed
        <time datetime={isoDate(changed)}>{longDate(changed)}</time>.
      </p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads nothing from other companies. If you choose light or dark
        with the switch at the top of the page, your browser remembers that choice on your device. It is not sent
        anywhere. If any of this changes, I will change this page and date it.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        Netlify hosts the site. Like any host, it may keep server logs, such as IP addresses and the pages requested.
        Its own <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> covers those logs.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        The signup box sends your email address to Substack, which sends the newsletter. Substack’s <a href="https://substack.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> covers what it holds.
      </p>

      <h2>Email to me</h2>
      <p>
        If you email me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, I get your address and what you write. I use
        it to reply and for nothing else.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
